     "text": "{\"count\":3,\"rationale\":\"crown:obtain is an OR of three paths: h4_1:reach, h4_2:access and h4_0:obtain. Every one of them must be cut. (1) h4_1:reach comes only from h2_2:access, which comes from the entry edge1:reach. One block (h2_2:access or h4_1:reach) is needed, and it does nothing for the other two paths. (2) h4_2:access is an OR of h2_1:obtain and h3_1:access. Cutting it takes either blocking h4_2:access itself, which leaves h4_0:obtain open and needs another block, or cutting both of its feeders. Either way at least 2 blocks cover h4_2:access and h4_0:obtain together. So 2 blocks is not enough. Three blocks work: h2_2:access, h3_1:access and h2_1:obtain. Blocking h3_1:access also cuts the AND step h4_0:obtain. Minimum = 3.\"}"
    }
